<title>SPAIN: Spain's BBV set 25.9 pct rise in H1 attributable.</title>
<headline>Spain's BBV set 25.9 pct rise in H1 attributable.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Bilbao Vizcaya</p>
<p>gave on Thursday the following first half results</p>
<p>				 (billion pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable profit		 58.11  vs  46.15</p>
<p> Net profit				  83.05  vs  57.54</p>
<p> Pretax profit			    129.52  vs  88.41</p>
<p> Net interest income		    265.44  vs 200.12</p>
<p> Ordinary income			  393.19  vs 289.53</p>
<p> Operating income			 156.62  vs 116.51</p>
<p> Interest income		     722.15     vs    704.96</p>
<p> Interest expenses		   456.72     vs    504.84</p>
<p> Fees and commissions		 93.35     vs     64.23</p>
<p> Financial/trading income	   34.40     vs     25.19</p>
<p> Personnal costs		     143.52     vs    108.30</p>
<p> General administrative costs     67.60     vs     43.91</p>
<p> Depreciation			   21.49     vs     14.75</p>
<p> Other operating expenses	    3.96     vs	6.07</p>
<p>Net earnings from equity-accounted</p>
<p>    holdings			    16.22     vs     10.22</p>
<p> Gains on group trans.		29.94     vs	5.85</p>
<p> Net loan-loss provisions	   28.51     vs     34.89</p>
<p> Amortisation of godwill	    31.32     vs	5.09</p>
<p> Net extraordinary losses	   13.51     vs	2.43</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 8340</p>
</text>
